<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabuktigin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 942–<a href="/years/997">997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Sebüktigin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabuktigin was a Turkic slave commander who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> from 977 to 997, nominally for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a>, and founded the Ghaznavid dynasty. He extended his power over Bust and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> valley and repeatedly defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> Shahi king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayapala">Jayapala</a>, pushing his frontier towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> built the dynasty into an empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sabuktigin.jpg" alt="Sabuktigin" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_the_Ghaznavid_amir_Sabuktigin,_citing_the_Samanid_amir_Nuh_II_as_his_overlord._Date_unknown,_minted_at_Ghazna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
